    "specPath": "specs/038-structured-extraction/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "An amendment of approved specs 002, 003 and 036 (R-16), for #76 child B6. Two supported ways to turn free text into typed decision inputs, both keeping extracted values model-derived. Pattern A: the host extracts and submits snapshot entries with provenance `model-derived` and an optional producer identity (artifact, template digest, production time), recorded in evidence and lineage. Pattern B: an `extract` step, a model step of spec 037's bounded envelope, asks a backend for a typed record against a declared schema and vocabularies under an identified prompt template; every field is validated and is present or absent with a reason, never coerced, clamped or truncated; each field carries its origin (`extracted`, `fallback`, `absent`) and derivation; a deterministic in-core fallback extractor (`rustev.extract-rules/1`) yields exact-derived fields; per-field distributions exist only from backend log-probabilities and are thresholded only under a bound calibration or a declared `uncalibrated_threshold`. In both patterns an exact operator, policy predicate, proposal parameter, acquisition request or other model step reads a model value only through a declared acceptance rule (an `accept_model_derived` step, or a spec 033 check covering `model-derived`); selection-policy controls never read one. Extraction can drive spec 033's `needs_input` outcome and propose which declared questions it asks. Adds to the shared #76 versions; every version 1 definition keeps its bytes, its plan and its `PlanId`. Approved (A-35); implementation is in progress.\n",
    "title": "Structured extraction step and the model-derived input pattern (amends 002, 003 and 036)"
  },
